From: Luca Stefani (LineageOS d8d35412206737bb3c84e157b5bd82609a835117)
Subject: [PATCH] gpuwork: Don't abort in case map doesn't exist

On /e/ v4.4-a16 (LineageOS 23.0) gpuservice aborts 30 seconds after
every start, so it crash-loops for as long as the phone runs. doha's
4.14 kernel doesn't get the gpuWork BPF maps, and 23.0's
GpuWork::initialize opens them with the BpfMap(path) constructor, which
aborts when the path is missing. LineageOS 23.2 already has this fix:
BpfMap::init() returns an error instead, and gpuwork then just stays
off. Applies unchanged to 23.0.

diff --git a/services/gpuservice/gpuwork/GpuWork.cpp b/services/gpuservice/gpuwork/GpuWork.cpp
index 4ad758a974..ccd5f3690e 100644
--- a/services/gpuservice/gpuwork/GpuWork.cpp
+++ b/services/gpuservice/gpuwork/GpuWork.cpp
@@ -67,12 +67,11 @@ bool equalGpuIdUid(const android::gpuwork::GpuIdUid& l, const android::gpuwork::
 template <class Key, class Value>
 bool getBpfMap(const char* mapPath, bpf::BpfMap<Key, Value>* out) {
     errno = 0;
-    auto map = bpf::BpfMap<Key, Value>(mapPath);
-    if (!map.isValid()) {
+    auto result = out->init(mapPath);
+    if (!result.ok()) {
         ALOGW("Failed to create bpf map from %s [%d(%s)]", mapPath, errno, strerror(errno));
         return false;
     }
-    *out = std::move(map);
     return true;
 }
 
